Subject: [PATCH] adbd: make fs_config opt-in on non-Android builds

should_use_fs_config() exists to restrict Android's fs_config-based
ownership/mode table to the partitions it actually describes
(/system, /vendor, /oem), with a compatibility carve-out that also
excludes /data on older on-device Android API levels. That carve-out
is guarded by `#if defined(__ANDROID__)`, so on a non-Android (Linux
host) build of adbd it never applies, and the function unconditionally
returns true instead.

As a result, every `adb push` destination -- including arbitrary
paths under /data -- gets routed through fs_config's android_dirs/
android_files tables. Those tables define a catch-all directory entry
for "data" (mode 0771, uid/gid AID_SYSTEM) but no equivalent catch-all
file entry, so a freshly pushed directory and the file inside it end
up with different, Android-partition-image-derived owners instead of
both simply being owned by whoever ran the push. Mode 0771 also means
a process that isn't root or system can traverse such a directory but
not list its contents, which breaks any non-privileged service trying
to iterate a pushed directory tree.

fs_config's table has nothing meaningful to say about a generic Linux
rootfs, so on non-Android builds disable it by default, which makes adbd
honour the mode sent by the host and leave ownership untouched. Builds
that do rely on fs_config can define ADBD_USE_FS_CONFIG, in which case
it is applied only to /system, /vendor and /oem.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Etienne Cordonnier <ecordonnier@snap.com>
---
 packages/modules/adb/daemon/file_sync_service.cpp | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/file_sync_service.cpp b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/file_sync_service.cpp
--- a/packages/modules/adb/daemon/file_sync_service.cpp
+++ b/packages/modules/adb/daemon/file_sync_service.cpp
@@ -81,8 +81,19 @@ static bool should_use_fs_config([[maybe_unused]] const std::string& path) {
     if (android_get_device_api_level() < __ANDROID_API_V__) {
         return !android::base::StartsWith(path, "/data/");
     }
-#endif
     return true;
+#elif defined(ADBD_USE_FS_CONFIG)
+    // Non-Android (Linux host) build with fs_config enabled: its tables only
+    // describe the system partitions, so keep it scoped to those rather than
+    // letting it apply to arbitrary pushed paths such as /data.
+    return android::base::StartsWith(path, "/system/") ||
+           android::base::StartsWith(path, "/vendor/") ||
+           android::base::StartsWith(path, "/oem/");
+#else
+    // Non-Android build, fs_config disabled: use the mode sent by the host and
+    // don't change ownership.
+    return false;
+#endif
 }
 
 static bool update_capabilities(const char* path, uint64_t capabilities) {
